      "answer": "Based on the web search results, I can provide information about the quaystone library's retry ceiling change:\n\nAccording to the search results, version 4.2.0 of the quaystone library changed how the retry ceiling counts. The changelog indicates this was a significant change in the library's retry mechanism.\n\nHowever, I cannot access the specific documentation or source code from this workspace to provide more detailed information about what exactly changed in that version. The workspace only contains a README, architecture documentation, and some configuration files, but no actual quaystone library code or changelog files that would show the specific implementation details of this change.\n\nThe search results indicate that:\n1. There was a version 4.2.0 that changed how retry ceiling counts\n2. This was documented in the quaystone changelog\n3. The change was significant enough to be noted in upgrade documentation\n\nBut without access to the actual library source code or its changelog files in this workspace, I cannot provide more specific details about what exactly changed in the retry mechanism between versions.",
